# Vauxhall Cadet saloon, 1930-1933.
#
# The Cadet: a 2,048 cc six announced on 6 October 1930, and the first
# British car with a synchromesh gearbox, fitted to all Cadets from late
# 1931. The saloon is modelled; the two-seater, the sports and four-light
# coupes, the Grosvenor, Tickford and Romney bodies and the panel van are not
# represented. The saloon body is SIX-light, with three windows per side,
# as images 1 and 2 both show; the four-light reference in the brief was
# wrong.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vauxhall_Cadet
#
# Dimensions: wheelbase 107 in (2.718 m), track 56 in. Length and height were
# not established from a source and are estimated from the photograph; the
# estimate is recorded.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a true level profile within about 2 degrees,
# with the wheel centres and the running board horizontal.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no Vauxhall colour list was found. Black, Maroon, Cream
# and Dark Blue are observed colours. Weights 12, 10, 9, 8, total 39,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 100 km/h. Comfort 25/368, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 25. Classes 2,3.
# Dates: intro October 1930; retires staggered 1947-1950 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-cadet.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/vauxhall-cadet.dae. References:
# citycars/references/vauxhall-cadet/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the six-light VY saloon is modelled. The VX side spare,
# the luggage and the taller radiator are not copied. The estimated length
# includes the empty luggage rack; the rear bumper ends at 4.04 m.


